	<section id="overview" class="main-content container">
					<div class="main-content__intro">
				<p><strong>&#8220;I want an adventure while I still can! And it&#8217;s gonna be scary and fun and really stupid&#8221;</strong></p>

			</div>
		
					<div class="main-content__text">
				<div data-olk-copy-source="MessageBody">
<p>Don&#8217;t miss the &#8216;astonishing&#8217; (<em>WhatsOnStage</em>) UK premiere of five-time Tony Award-winning musical <em>Kimberly Akimbo</em>, starring the &#8216;superb&#8217; (<em>Financial Times</em>) <strong>Maria Friedman</strong>!</p>
<p>Kimberly Levaco is excited to celebrate her upcoming sweet 16 – never mind the fact she looks 74, due to a rare genetic condition prematurely ageing her about four times faster than her friends. Whilst her heart may be biologically ahead of its time, it’s starting to beat a little quicker after meeting Seth at the ice rink…</p>
<p>Kim doesn’t have long to explore the world beyond New Jersey, she just needs to find the cash to do it. When her ex-con aunt shows up with a get-rich-quick scam, Kim’s all in – illegal or not. Can she pull off the heist, find first love and have the great adventures she&#8217;s been dreaming of?</p>
<p><strong>David Lindsay-Abaire</strong> (<em>Good People</em>) and <strong>Jeanine Tesori</strong>&#8216;s (<em>Caroline, or Change</em>) profoundly funny and heartwarming musical was the winner of five 2023 Tony Awards including Best Musical. This much-anticipated new production by <strong>Michael Longhurst</strong> (<em>Next to Normal</em>) stars one of the most acclaimed performers in musical theatre, Maria Friedman, as Kimberly. She is a four-time Olivier Award winner, with nine nominations and a Tony nomination.</p>
<p>Thank you to the<em> Kimberly Akimbo</em> Giving Circle for generously supporting the production: Ken &amp; Lin Craig; Luce &amp; Jean-Charles Julien; Nicola Kerr; Pamela, Lady Harlech; Carol &amp; Gary Fethke; Leigh &amp; Lena Collins; Sheri &amp; Daryl Orts; Claire Tremeer &amp; Bob Reichert; Sophie &amp; Stephen Warshaw; Gerry Wakelin; Gillian King and Kay &amp; Jim Ashton</p>
</div>

			</div>
			</section>

		<div class="wrapper__details">

